From 173e586612b85e211fec2655586a53c674f12867 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John R Reeves III <johnreevesiii@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:10:13 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] linkbus: hub learns the slot size from the master (review
 R1, R2)

Review R1 (delta review of c9be11a7c): InMemoryHub learned the slot size
from whichever bound seat sent first, so a seat that sent a valid frame
with a different slot size first locked out the honest seats as BadSize.
The hub now learns it only from the master's (node 0) first accepted
frame. A satellite frame that arrives before it is refused as BadSize,
counted in the new InMemoryHub::Stats::beforeMaster (also in badSize),
and not recorded, so its localFrame is still new later.

Review R2 (documentation only): the linkbus_web.cpp header said that
Multiboard falls back to its default when the cabinet buffer is too
small. In fact makeSabMultiboardBackend returns nullptr and the
Multiboard constructor throws "Cannot initialize Naomi multiboard
LinkBus backend"; under Emscripten there is no default.

Tests: four hub tests now send a master frame first; new test
reviewR1_hub_learns_slot_size_from_master (31 tests, 4185 checks).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MGX7KQ5gfrWApgW64pZbQ5
